{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795021730,"nonce":"JiQFp2tv8iRRlHpvHqPG9jRBYi0=","target":"eb1b66f252597b748df426ca19f7433d0d94ec7af41d2e58e1598130b2a4c5db","message":"## Problem Statement\n\nThe grow page answers \"how are my plants doing?\" in fragments. Live environment tiles and the history charts live under separate headings, so \"what's the reading now\" and \"what did it do this week\" are two places. The history itself renders as eight sibling chart cards, each with its own 24h/7d/30d window toggle: eight controls to click, eight fetches, eight time axes that can silently disagree. Charts for roles the grow never bound still take up space with \"no data\" ghosts. The day/night rhythm — the single most important pattern in a grow room — is invisible unless the reader mentally overlays the light card onto the temperature card. Watering and feeding events are not on the charts at all, even though correlating them with soil moisture, pH and EC is exactly why those charts exist (spec §4.9 requires log events overlaid as markers; this was never implemented). And the page opens on the harvest forecast, not on the environment the owner checks at the tent every morning.\n\n## Solution\n\nOne **Environment section** on the grow page: the existing live tiles as its top row, and beneath them a single instrument panel of history charts. One shared window control (24h/7d/30d, defaulting to 7 days, remembered per browser) drives every chart with aligned time axes and a shared crosshair — hover anywhere, read temperature, humidity and VPD at the same instant. Charts group into **Air** (temperature, humidity, VPD, CO₂) and **Root zone** (soil moisture, pH, EC), both terms glossary-defined. The day/night cycle becomes a subtle night tint behind the Air charts (observed light-entity behaviour where bound, the editable Light Cycle as fallback), replacing the standalone Light card. Role-relevant log events appear as quiet tick marks — watering/feed/repot on Root zone charts, light transitions and phase picks on Air — with a section-header toggle to hide them. Temperature charts gain a Target Band derived from the grow's heat/cold tolerances and VPD charts a phase-appropriate band that steps between day and night ranges, both engine-sourced. Only bound roles render charts; unbound roles collapse into one quiet \"not measured\" card with a bind affordance. The Root zone group renders lazily when scrolled into view. The page order becomes: header/logging loop, Environment, Forecast, Feed, Timeline, Plants, Photos. All of this stays inside the incumbent Cultivation Bench design system — palette untouched (owner-endorsed; it tracks the Home Assistant theme), flat tonal depth, no new chrome hues.\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. As the grow owner, I want the live environment tiles and the history charts in one section, so that \"how are they now\" and \"what did they do\" are one glance, not two headings.\n2. As the grow owner, I want one window control for all charts, so that I never see humidity for a week next to temperature for a day.\n3. As the grow owner, I want the window to default to 7 days, so that the day/night rhythm is visible without touching anything.\n4. As the grow owner, I want my chosen window remembered per browser, so that returning to the page shows the span I actually use.\n5. As the grow owner, I want a shared crosshair across all charts, so that I can read temperature, humidity and VPD at the same instant.\n6. As the grow owner, I want charts grouped as Air and Root zone, so that I can scan the concerns I came for without scrolling past unrelated metrics.\n7. As the grow owner, I want per-card window toggles gone, so that the section reads as one instrument panel, not eight widgets.\n8. As the grow owner, I want night periods shaded behind the Air charts, so that the photoperiod rhythm explains the temperature and humidity waves without mental overlay.\n9. As the grow owner, I want the shading to follow what my light entity actually did (with the editable cycle as fallback), so that gaps and overrides are honest.\n10. As the grow owner, I want a legend hint for the night tint, so that the shading is never mystery grey.\n11. As the grow owner, I want watering, feed and repot events as tick marks on the Root zone charts, so that I can see the cause next to the effect on soil moisture, pH and EC.\n12. As the grow owner, I want light transitions and phase picks as tick marks on the Air charts, so that \"why did the environment jump\" is answered on the chart itself.\n13. As the grow owner, I want a markers on/off toggle in the section header, so that I can get clean lines when I don't need the events.\n14. As the grow owner, I want each marker's tooltip to name the event, so that a tick is never ambiguous.\n15. As the grow owner, I want a Target Band behind my temperature chart derived from the grow's heat/cold tolerances, so that \"hot for this grow\" is drawn, not remembered.\n16. As the grow owner, I want a phase-appropriate Target Band behind my VPD chart that steps between day and night ranges, so that a novice-safe reading is available without knowing VPD tables.\n17. As the grow owner, I want only bound roles to render charts, so that the panel shows what my grow actually measures.\n18. As the grow owner, I want unbound roles collected in one quiet \"not measured\" card with a bind affordance, so that adding a sensor is one tap away without eight \"no data\" ghosts.\n19. As the grow owner, I want honest empty-window hints on bound roles, so that a gap in data never silently pretends to be zero or fine.\n20. As the grow owner checking the tent on a low-end phone, I want the Root zone charts to render when scrolled into view, so that first paint stays fast.\n21. As the grow owner, I want the Environment section above the forecast, so that the page opens on what I check daily, not what I plan once.\n22. As the grow owner using the dark theme, I want every new element to work in both themes, so that neither theme is second-class.\n23. As a German-speaking grow owner, I want all new UI strings in English and German, so that the section reads natively in my locale.\n24. As the grow owner, I want compact uniform chart heights, so that seven charts scan as one panel instead of an endless scroll.\n25. As the grow owner with a wide screen, I want charts two-up on large viewports, so that the panel shortens the scroll.\n\n## Implementation Decisions\n\n- Section redesign inside the incumbent Cultivation Bench design system; palette, tokens and themes untouched. DESIGN.md's \"tolerated, not loved\" palette verdict is refreshed to record owner endorsement (the palette tracks the Home Assistant theme).\n- The page section order becomes: header/logging loop, Environment, Forecast, Feed, Timeline, Plants, Photos. Live env tiles remain visually unchanged, relocated as the section's top row.\n- One shared window state (24h/7d/30d; default 7d) persisted in localStorage drives every chart; the segmented control reserves room for a future fourth \"whole grow\" position but shows no disabled teaser.\n- Chart groups: Air (temperature, humidity, VPD, CO₂) and Root zone (soil moisture, pH, EC). \"Air\" and \"Root zone\" become glossary terms. Charts remain separate single-axis series per role (no dual-axis combination).\n- Crosshair sync via an ECharts connect group across the section's charts; each chart keeps a compact tooltip limited to its own role's value.\n- The standalone Light chart card is retired; photoperiod becomes night shading (markArea) behind Air charts, sourced from the light role series with observed-entity-on/off overriding the editable Light Cycle for gaps and the future. A legend hint explains the tint.\n- The existing per-role history API response gains a role-relevant log-event markers array (watering/feed/repot for root-zone roles; light transitions and phase picks for air roles), rendered as one quiet vertical tick glyph with tooltip naming the event; a section-header toggle hides markers. No new endpoints.\n- Target Bands (existing soil-moisture machinery) extend to temperature (derived from the grow's heat/cold tolerances) and VPD (phase-appropriate, stepping between day and night ranges per the existing Target Band semantics). Both are engine-sourced; no invented ranges. pH, EC and CO₂ stay bare.\n- Bound-role visibility: only roles with bindings (or log-detail data) render chart cards; unbound roles appear in one compact \"not measured\" card listing role chips with a bind affordance. Dead bindings keep their card with a degraded banner (existing behaviour preserved).\n- Root zone group lazy-renders via IntersectionObserver with an immediate-render fallback when unavailable.\n- Charts drop per-card toggle rows; uniform compact heights (~150px mobile / ~180px desktop); two-up grid on large viewports.\n- All styling through existing daisyUI semantic roles; no new hues in chrome (Phase Accent Rule); markers and shading are geometry, not colour.\n- A reserved slot for a whole-grow window is designed-in but not implemented; HA history API backfill remains out of scope.\n\n## Testing Decisions\n\n- Good tests assert external behaviour only: the history API response's shape and marker contents for a seeded grow with snapshots and log events; the pure ECharts option builder's output structure for shading bands, marker ticks and connect-group settings; and browser-level behaviour of the section (window control drives all charts, groups render, markers toggle, unbound card appears, lazy render) against the mock HA.\n- The per-role history API contract is tested at the existing backend integration seam (seed grow + snapshots + action log, then assert response fields, marker selection per role, and window filtering).\n- The chart option builder stays pure Rust and unit-tested in-crate (prior art: its existing unit tests).\n- E2E Playwright specs extend the existing environment-charts and temperature-chart specs' patterns; screenshots verify both themes at desktop and mobile viewports against the design system.\n- EN/DE key parity rides the existing CI parity gate.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Whole-grow chart window (data and UI) — only its reserved control position.\n- HA history API backfill for windows older than local snapshots.\n- Live env tile redesign.\n- Palette or token revision of any kind.\n- Structural changes to Forecast, Feed, Timeline, Plants or Photos beyond the reorder and consistency sweep.\n- New chart types beyond line charts with shading/markers/bands.\n\n## Further Notes\n\n- Source plan: three grilling rounds confirmed in-session (2026-11-18); all decisions above were explicitly approved by the owner, including palette endorsement and the DESIGN.md verdict-line refresh.\n- Spec references: docs/SPEC.md §4.9 (grow dashboard chart list with log-event markers), Target Band and Light Cycle definitions in GLOSSARY.md, DESIGN.md (Cultivation Bench rules).","files":null}]}